# SFT execution status v0.123: corrected native AWS rehearsal passed

2026-09-27 (Dhaka). **The failed-attempt launcher defect is fixed and the
fresh generated-only Linux recovery passed all four native cases.** Gate 5
as a whole is not complete: no real 4B checkpoint import or SFT run is claimed.

The user approved a fresh bounded AWS CPU attempt after the v0.122 failure.
Exactly one new `t3.large` VM and one fresh attempt were used. No test retry,
resource-limit increase, model-source change or old evidence overwrite occurred.

## Verified fix and results

The v3 entry loads the stdlib-only control file directly, avoiding the eager
ML registration in `lumi/__init__.py`. On the actual Linux runtime, an import
guard rejected any attempt to load lumi/torch/transformers/numpy/safetensors.
Control loading, source verification and host checks passed with **zero such
imports and 20,476 KiB maximum RSS**. Thus the small resource probes no longer
import ML before reaching their boundary checks. The fixed chain child alone
imports ML from exact worker-owned source copies in its private tmpfs.

| Native case | Unchanged limit | Accepted result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Generated import/package chain | 2 GiB, 120 s | Four actual tiny DCP/import/package/checksum/reload tests passed |
| Timeout with child | 128 MiB, 2 s | systemd timeout; independent observer saw two processes; empty cgroup afterward |
| Memory allocation | 96 MiB, 15 s | systemd OOM kill; empty cgroup afterward |
| Storage exhaustion | 256 MiB RAM, 64-MiB tmpfs, 15 s | Fixed worker accepted ENOSPC only after at least 63 MiB written; successful exit; empty cgroup afterward |

The launcher retained `passed_generated_only`, all four case results, and no
failure record. The read-only observer collected counts/counters, never PID
values, source text, exception text or worker logs. Its sampled chain memory
maximum was 286,035,968 bytes and timeout process-count maximum was two. The
fast memory/disk probes can complete between 50-ms samples: these samples are
not exhaustive peaks or an independent observation of ENOSPC. Their acceptance
comes from the unchanged pinned probe code plus systemd terminal outcomes.

All four cgroups were independently confirmed empty after cleanup. The entire
root-owned source release was hash-verified again after the run. The exact
started/result records were copied and their remote/local SHA-256 values matched.

