## Runtime, setup and cleanup

The working final-stage bootstrap v0.3 was reused. Its active/waiting one-hour
boot-relative expiry was verified before staging and dispatch. Ubuntu 24.04 /
systemd 255 / signed-apt Python 3.12.3 plus 34 hash-pinned CPU wheels were used:
torch 2.14.0+cpu, transformers 5.15.1, safetensors 0.8.0, tokenizers 0.22.2 and
numpy 2.5.3. The 248,715,637 software-download bytes were not model data.
This is still not the old OCI image identity; that distinction is preserved.

Only an authenticated HTTPS Instance Connect tunnel could reach SSH; no public
SSH ingress rule was added. The VM had no IAM instance profile, required IMDSv2,
and used a 20-GiB encrypted, delete-on-termination disk. The setup command was
initially rejected by the workspace's automatic approval review because of
credits; it did not execute. After the user reported refill, the same setup
ran once. This was not a native attempt retry or approval bypass.

The VM is confirmed **terminated**, its EBS volume is absent, the tunnel is
`delete-complete`, and both temporary security groups and the AWS key
registration are absent. No pre-existing resource was modified. Ephemeral
VM files are deleted and not recoverable, while exact run records, source
archives and aggregate evidence remain in git-ignored local artifacts. No
training instance is left running for this task.

## Local verification and remaining work

The final local run passed **45 tests, zero failures/errors/skips**: 37 control/
source-copy tests, two stdlib-entry regressions, three bootstrap tests and three
aggregate-observer tests. Ruff passed. The extracted source archive's 41 files
were verified, and its control entry loaded without ML independently of the repo.
The prior failed marker/result evidence and frozen model/import/package/SFT
sources remain unchanged. No commit or push was performed.

This closes the **four-case generated-only native rehearsal blocker**, not all
possible production isolation properties. In particular, no controller-death
exercise or cumulative-native-write cap is claimed. The launcher itself reports
that billing/shutdown management is external; this run's operator separately
verified expiry and performed cleanup.

Next Gate-5 work remains the host-bound real-input/full-size coordinator adapter
and the independently verified real checkpoint import from the preserved S3
pretraining lineage. This run accessed no real checkpoint, tokenizer or dataset.
Gate 6 still requires training-specific approval, GPU smoke/save/resume checks
and the SFT run, followed by evaluation and serving gates. GPU use, inference,
training and production eligibility remain false here.

